After Pure Idle launched, the fairest criticism it received was the one I wrote about in Part 3: the technology tree was wide but shallow, hundreds of nodes that were really one idea. I agreed. And the honest response to “your variety is fake” is not to argue — it is to go build some variety that is real. That is where the warehouse came from: a subsystem I added after release, in which I quietly built a small role-playing game inside a game about dropping stars into a black hole.
This part is about that warehouse — the most out-of-character system in the whole clicker, and my favorite thing in it.
You can read the first part of this article here.
Author: Aleksei Makarenko. Pen names: Alex Vuorenmaa, Riven Elow.
